window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-b790d9afda421b3c"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"qa-your-app-with-computer-use\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"computer-use\">使用 Computer Use 测试应用</h1> <p>走查真实产品流程，记录问题。</p> <p>使用 Computer Use 演练关键流程、发现功能或界面问题，并生成一份缺陷报告。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>发布前验证真实用户流程的团队</li> <li>需要按严重程度和复现步骤整理问题，并给出简短分诊总结的 QA 测试</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">起步提示词</h2> <p>执行结构化 QA 测试</p> <p>建议模型：<code>gpt-6.1-sol</code> · 建议推理级别：<code>xhigh</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">@Computer 请在 [environment] 环境中测试我的应用。\n\n请测试以下流程：\n- [hero use case 1]\n- [hero use case 2]\n- [hero use case 3]\n\n对于发现的每个缺陷，请写明：\n- 复现步骤\n- 预期结果\n- 实际结果\n- 严重程度\n\n不要因为遇到非阻塞问题就停止；继续完成其余测试，并以简短的问题分诊总结收尾。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7be3f970bd43699c\">Computer Use</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">技能</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"introduction\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">简介</h2> <p>Computer Use 很适合用于 QA 测试：它可以查看界面、点击操作流程、在输入框中输入内容，并记录失败之处。因此，它能帮助你在贴近真实使用的流程中发现功能缺陷和界面问题。</p> <p>关键是告诉 Codex 要测试哪个环境、哪些流程最重要，以及你希望它用什么形式报告结果。</p> <p><a id=\"how-to-use\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">使用方法</h2> <ol> <li>安装 <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/computer-use\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Computer Use 插件（本地尚未收录）</a>。</li> <li>告诉 Codex 要测试哪个应用、构建版本或环境。</li> <li>列出你最关心的流程或核心用例。</li> <li>要求它按固定结构报告，便于你分诊或交接问题。</li> </ol> <p>你可以先用较宽泛的要求：</p> <ul> <li><code>@Computer Test my app. Find any major issues and give me a report.</code></li> </ul> <p>也可以把要求说得更具体：</p> <ul> <li><code>@Computer Test my app in staging. Cover signup, invite a teammate, and upgrade billing. Log every bug with repro steps, expected result, actual result, and severity.</code></li> </ul> <p>如果你已经在代码库中维护测试计划文件，可以把它附加到对话，或告诉 Codex 文件位置，让本次测试遵循现有流程。</p> <p><a id=\"practical-tips\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">实用技巧</h2> <p><a id=\"be-explicit-about-setup\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_7\">明确测试环境</h3> <p>如果账户状态、测试数据、功能开关或环境选择会影响流程，请一开始就说明。让 Codex 知道它测试的是本地、预发布还是接近生产的环境，结果会更可靠。</p> <p><a id=\"name-the-issue-types-you-care-about\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_8\">指明要关注的问题类型</h3> <p>说明你希望 Codex 关注功能故障、布局问题、令人困惑的文案、视觉回归，还是以上全部问题。</p> <p><a id=\"decide-whether-to-stop-or-continue\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_9\">决定遇到问题时是停止还是继续</h3> <p>如果某个阻塞问题一出现就应结束测试，请明确说明。否则，请让 Codex 继续完成其它流程，并收集所有非阻塞问题后再总结。</p> <p><a id=\"good-follow-ups\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_10\">后续可以怎么做</h2> <p>完成 QA 测试后，可以继续在同一对话中让 Codex 修复发现的问题、把结论整理成适合提交到 Linear 或 GitHub 的草稿，或把下一轮测试缩小到某个失败流程。</p> <p><a id=\"suggested-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_11\">建议提示词</h2> <p><strong>执行结构化 QA 测试</strong></p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">@Computer Test my app in [environment].\n\nTest these flows:\n\n- [hero use case 1]\n- [hero use case 2]\n- [hero use case 3]\n\nFor every bug you find, include:\n\n- repro steps\n- expected result\n- actual result\n- severity\n\nKeep going past non-blocking issues and end with a short triage summary.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">@Computer 请在 [environment] 中测试我的应用。\n\n测试以下流程：\n\n- [hero use case 1]\n- [hero use case 2]\n- [hero use case 3]\n\n对于发现的每个缺陷，包括：\n\n- 复现步骤\n- 预期结果\n- 实际结果\n- 严重程度\n\n遇到非阻断性问题时继续测试，最后给出简短的分流摘要。</div></div>","en":"<h1 id=\"qa-your-app-with-computer-use\">QA your app with Computer Use</h1> <p>Click through real product flows and log what breaks.</p> <p>Use Computer Use to exercise key flows, catch issues, and finish with a bug report.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Teams validating real user flows before a release</li> <li>QA loops that should end with severity, repro steps, and a short triage summary</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Run a Structured QA Pass</p> <p>Suggested model：<code>gpt-6.1-sol</code> · Suggested reasoning effort：<code>xhigh</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">@Computer Test my app in [environment].\n\nTest these flows:\n- [hero use case 1]\n- [hero use case 2]\n- [hero use case 3]\n\nFor every bug you find, include:\n- repro steps\n- expected result\n- actual result\n- severity\n\nKeep going past non-blocking issues and end with a short triage summary.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7be3f970bd43699c\">Computer Use</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">Skills</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"introduction\">Introduction</h2> <p>Computer Use is a strong fit for QA passes because it can see the interface, click through flows, type into fields, and record what fails. That makes it useful for catching both functional bugs and UI issues across realistic user journeys.</p> <p>The key is to tell Codex what environment to test, which flows matter most, and what kind of report you want back.</p> <h2 id=\"how-to-use\">How to use</h2> <ol> <li>Install the <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/computer-use\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Computer Use plugin (not in this local snapshot)</a>.</li> <li>Tell Codex which app, build, or environment to test.</li> <li>Name the flows or hero use cases you care about most.</li> <li>Ask for a structured report so the output is easy to triage or hand off.</li> </ol> <p>You can keep this broad:</p> <ul> <li><code>@Computer Test my app. Find any major issues and give me a report.</code></li> </ul> <p>Or make it more explicit:</p> <ul> <li><code>@Computer Test my app in staging. Cover signup, invite a teammate, and upgrade billing. Log every bug with repro steps, expected result, actual result, and severity.</code></li> </ul> <p>If you already maintain a test-plan file in the repo, attach it to the chat or point Codex at it so the QA pass follows your existing flows.</p> <h2 id=\"practical-tips\">Practical tips</h2> <h3 id=\"be-explicit-about-setup\">Be explicit about setup</h3> <p>If account state, test data, feature flags, or environment choice affect the flow, include that up front. Codex will produce much better results when it knows whether it is testing local, staging, or production-like behavior.</p> <h3 id=\"name-the-issue-types-you-care-about\">Name the issue types you care about</h3> <p>Call out whether you want Codex to focus on broken functionality, layout issues, confusing copy, visual regressions, or all of the above.</p> <h3 id=\"decide-whether-to-stop-or-continue\">Decide whether to stop or continue</h3> <p>If one blocking issue should end the run, say so. Otherwise, tell Codex to continue through the rest of the flow and collect all non-blocking issues before it summarizes.</p> <h2 id=\"good-follow-ups\">Good follow-ups</h2> <p>After the QA pass, keep the same chat open and ask Codex to fix one of the bugs it found, turn the findings into Linear or GitHub-ready drafts, or narrow the next pass to one specific failing flow.</p> <h2 id=\"suggested-prompt\">Suggested prompt</h2> <p><strong>Run a Structured QA Pass</strong></p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">@Computer Test my app in [environment].\n\nTest these flows:\n\n- [hero use case 1]\n- [hero use case 2]\n- [hero use case 3]\n\nFor every bug you find, include:\n\n- repro steps\n- expected result\n- actual result\n- severity\n\nKeep going past non-blocking issues and end with a short triage summary.\n</code></pre>"};
